{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:PredictedSpectra.GammaGammaGeneratesParticles","@type":"LeanModule","name":"PredictedSpectra.GammaGammaGeneratesParticles","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":5,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.GammaGammaGeneration.gamma_gamma_reaches_Lminus","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.GammaGammaGeneration.gamma_gamma_reaches_Lminus","kind":"theorem","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/gamma-gamma-generates-particles.lean#L52-L60","doc":"**γγ production strictly enlarges the reachable operator set.**\nThere are photon color weights whose two-photon product carries a\nnonzero `L₋ = σ₁σ₀` operator — content no single photon can hold. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.GammaGammaGeneration.singlePhotonCoeffLminus","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.GammaGammaGeneration.singlePhotonCoeffLminus","kind":"def","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/gamma-gamma-generates-particles.lean#L47-L50","doc":"The `L₋ = σ₁σ₀` content of a *single* photon\n`γ = 𝟙 + φ₀σ₀ + φ₁σ₁ + φ₀₁σ₀σ₁` is zero: its support is\n`{𝟙, σ₀, σ₁, σ₀σ₁}`, which does not include `σ₁σ₀`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.GammaGammaGeneration.gamma_gamma_chirality_surjective","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.GammaGammaGeneration.gamma_gamma_chirality_surjective","kind":"theorem","line":37,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/gamma-gamma-generates-particles.lean#L37-L45","doc":"**The chiral pair is generated independently by γγ production.**\nFor any target pair `(a, b)` there exist photon color weights whose\ntwo-photon product has `L₊`-coefficient `a` and `L₋`-coefficient `b`\n(take `φ₀ = a, ψ₁ = 1, φ₁ = b, ψ₀ = 1`).  Hence both chiral Hopf\noperators arise from `γγ` production. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:gamma-gamma-generates-particles","label":"prop:gamma-gamma-generates-particles","md":"quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/gamma-gamma-generates-particles.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.GammaGammaGeneration.coeffLminus","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.GammaGammaGeneration.coeffLminus","kind":"def","line":34,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/gamma-gamma-generates-particles.lean#L34-L35","doc":"Coefficient of `L₋ = σ₁σ₀` in the two-photon product: `φ₁ · ψ₀`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.GammaGammaGeneration.coeffLplus","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.GammaGammaGeneration.coeffLplus","kind":"def","line":29,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/gamma-gamma-generates-particles.lean#L29-L32","doc":"Coefficient of `L₊ = σ₀σ₁` in the two-photon product `γ₁·γ₂`, as a\nfunction of the color weights `(φ₀, φ₁)` of `γ₁` and `(ψ₀, ψ₁)` of\n`γ₂`: the cross-color product `φ₀ · ψ₁`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}